  "preamble": "The alveolar tap [ɾ] loses its brief closure and is realized as the alveolar approximant [ɹ]. In Persian, [ɹ] is an allophone of /ɾ/ before /t, d, s, z, ʃ, ʒ, l/, varying freely with the tap, especially in western Iranian Persian. Comparable weakening of the tap to [ɹ] is reported for Albanian, Catalan (post-vocalic, in Valencian and Balearic), Modern Greek (between vowels in rapid speech) and Marmara Turkish (coda).",
